  "metadata_synthesis": "Film. 2010. Darren Aronofsky. Natalie Portman. Mila Kunis. Ballet thriller. Psychological horror.",
  "setting_and_subculture": "High-stakes New York ballet. Cutthroat dance companies. Rehearsal studios bathed in sweat. Stage lights blindingly hot. Claustrophobic dressing rooms.",
  "visual_tone_and_feel": "Stark black and white contrasts. Feathers piercing skin. Hallucinatory mirrors. Handheld camera anxiety. Flashes of bloody wounds. Spinning, dizzying choreography.",
  "media_era_tone": "Late 2000s/early 2010s dark indie cinema. Unapologetic melodrama. Gritty reality crashing into surreal fantasy. Female unraveling as high art.",
  "pacing_and_structure": "Slow tightening of the noose. Paranoia building with every pirouette. Crescendo of madness. Explosive final act. A descent into beautiful chaos.",
  "atmosphere_and_mood": "Suffocating pressure. Fever dream logic. Darkly absurd. Intense, unyielding dread. Erotic tension laced with terror.",
  "themes_and_messages": "The price of perfection. Killing innocence to achieve greatness. Battling the self. Destructive obsession. Feminine madness. Duality of human nature.",
  "character_relationships": "Toxic mother-daughter control. Sapphic rivalries. The mirrored nemesis. Predator and prey blur. Obsession mirroring jealousy.",
  "lead_character_type": "High-strung perfectionist. Repressed ingénue cracking open. Unreliable narrator. The innocent swan consumed by the dark.",
  "story_and_plot_type": "Psychological thriller. Descent into madness. Artist destroying herself for the work. Doppelgänger terror. Tragic triumph.",
  "who_and_when": "Nina Sayers. Modern-day New York City. Ballet company staging Swan Lake.",
  "emotional_evocation": "Panic. Intoxicating horror. Claustrophobic empathy. Visceral cringe. Awe mixed with disgust. Tragic catharsis."
